"""Report and support-review instructions shared by the SDK workflow."""
DRAFT_INSTRUCTIONS = '\nNow produce the final cited draft report in the required schema. Every factual claim needs supporting exact excerpts. Keep conclusions qualified. Never claim intent or wrongdoing is established. Empty extracts and absence of restrictions are not evidence against misconduct. A lightweight case should have 2–4 concise observations. Treat absent authority or archive coverage as gaps, not proof the activity was unauthorized. Before returning: explicitly cite relevant unavailable records in gaps. Describe communication wording as an observed fact; label any proposed motive or price-influence explanation as an inference, not an instruction the source explicitly gives. During repair, change only rejected claims or missing gaps and preserve the already-supported observations; do not strengthen their wording or add new factual assertions.'
REVIEW_INSTRUCTIONS = 'You independently verify a surveillance draft against the supplied evidence only. Return supported=false for unsupported material claims, scope/timestamp errors, unwarranted accusations, treating missing evidence as exculpatory, or ignoring a material contradiction. Each rejection must identify an actual problematic statement: copy its exact full claim text from the report into flagged_claims and explain the issue. Do not reject a hypothetical statement that the draft does not make. A clearly qualified alternative explanation is not an assertion that it is proven; a gap explicitly acknowledging missing order-specific authority must not be criticized as asserting that authority exists. Do not demand proof that all imaginable hidden facts are absent. Set issues and flagged_claims to empty lists when supported. Exact citations alone do not prove support. Distinguish reasonable qualified hypotheses from factual conclusions. Questions must not smuggle unsupported facts. Reject claims that valuation-related wording explicitly instructs price influence or manipulation unless the supplied text actually makes that instruction. A comment about the importance of a valuation is not itself an explicit instruction to move a price. Do not accept broad exculpatory claims about absence of improper motive, confidential information or suspicious communications based on a mandate or limited extract. No hidden answer keys are available.'

REVIEW_INSTRUCTIONS += ' Live market_news records are retrospective search-generated summaries with unverified publication timing, not verbatim articles. Reject assertions based only on these records that information was available before a trade or cutoff, that no news existed, or that news proves knowledge, intent or causality. Qualified source-reported context with explicit timing uncertainty is acceptable.'
